Z||000000||cowans||07-25-2001||08:38 AM||||I am at my wits' end!!! I have an 85 GT F40 Replica and have upgraded the AC to 134a. The shop that did it replaced: compressor, compressor hoses & fittings, O-rings, leak detector, accumulator/drier, a $6 filter screen(located near the evaporater). They flushed the entire system and recharged 134a. Five miles down the road the compressor locked up, blowing up the compressor clutch. The shop warranted/replaced the compressor and recharged the system but at only 85/90% charge as they realised they may have overcharged the system 1st time around! The car ran for 30 minutes in their shop with the gauges on, compressor cycling normally. I take the car out last night, turn on the AC and within 2 miles the belt is squealing horribly, with the compressor locked up. I immediately turned off the AC, but I am entertaining any thoughts on WHY??? I have already booked a DIFFERENT SHOP to look into this problem, just need ideas. I have spent MUCHO $$$ so far (enough $$$$, that I can't stop now!!!)<BR>Help!!! Sandy||||reg||8
Z||000001||skitime||07-25-2001||09:13 AM||||All I can ask is why?  Why did you change everything. Probably bad advise from a greedy air conditioning shop.  We converted both of ours with only changing filling valves, having the system evacuated for 1 hour then recharging with the 134a.  They work great. Had my Grand Prix done the same 2 years ago and still running cold.  Cost $120 each from the AC shop.<P>------------------<BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>Red 88 GT T-TOP<BR><LI>Red 86 GT<BR></UL>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature-1.JPG">   <P><p>[This message has been edited by skitime (edited 07-25-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||88CoupeV6||07-25-2001||10:48 AM||||Did they add the oil, Sounds like there is no oil charged into the system  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg">   <BR><B>Also 88 Yellow GT</B> :D  <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||5
Z||000003||cowans||07-25-2001||11:55 AM||||The compressor from the donor car was dead, that's why the new compressor. Changed the compressor hoses on spect(my choice)as I didn't trust 15 yr old hoses!!! Yes, 134a oil (6oz) was added, o-rings changed, new orafice tube..... Their gauges showed proper #'s with compressor cycling.... and it seizes!!! System was FLUSHED!!! <BR>Sandy||||reg||1
Z||000004||voyagerspe||07-25-2001||10:07 PM||||assuming they did all that you said it sounds like the local parts warehouse has a bad batch of compressors.  Try to get the installers to get a compressor from a different source||||reg||1
Z||000005||Fiero_Freak||07-25-2001||10:29 PM||||   Are you sure it's locked up?  Driving with the new belt stretched mine out and just had to re-tighten it.  I just wasn't sure if you had checked it the second time.||||reg||1
